2 engines the Miura  conte and other later model Lamborghinis  didn't have much in common with the 350  GT it was the one Lamborghini that  managed to be both a devilishly fast  super car and an elegant Gran Turismo  that's all christo says the 350gt isn't  as flashy as Lamborghinis later more  spectacular models and it wasn't a big  seller either just 141 of them changed  hands between 1964 and 1967 still the  350 GT established Lamborghini as super  car maker and was unrivaled in its time  today at 350 GT in good condition will  set you back at least two hundred twenty  thousand euros around the same price  you'd pay for a Ferrari from the same  error next time on drive it sporty  performance meets timeless elegance the  new Porsche gt3 RS and a look at the sea  at me which runs on natural gas  you  you
 

